    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the clear priority play with an elite score of 83.29. His projection is bolstered by a potent combination of a favorable matchup against Severino (xERA 4.60) and a substantial 16% park factor boost. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.99) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.87) are high-efficiency starts; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% platoon edge against Alcantara, while **Jacob Wilson** is primed to exploit a generous park factor and a weak SP matchup. We are also looking for a significant performance from **Kyle Tucker** (69.76) and **Jackson Merrill** (66.29), both of whom offer reliable production despite the varying difficulty of their respective draws.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Nasim Nunez** (55.82). Despite his value as a stolen base asset, he was relegated to the bench because his projected efficiency is squeezed by his spot at the bottom of the order. While he would theoretically benefit from Alcantara's slow delivery to the plate\u2014a key indicator for our SB-heavy strategy\u2014his projected floor is lower than the high-upside plays of **Brady House** or **Josh Jung**. We are keeping a close eye on **Heliot Ramos** (50.81); while the wind blowing out provides a nice boost, his score is tempered by the risk of facing Chandler. Owners should be aware that **Liam Hicks** (52.72) and **Drake Baldwin** (53.28) remain marginal plays; while they are serviceable, they lack the ceiling of our top-tier hitters, and we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL and unavailable to bolster our lineup.",
